Keep guest loads whose value is not used (FEX 3bec2ac, on top of 0021)

An x86 load can fault, and programs load only for that: MSVC's _chkstk
touches each 4 KB page of a large frame with `test [ecx], eax`, flags
dead before the next instruction, so that the stack's guard page is hit
in order. In FEX's IR, LoadMem and LoadMemTSO had no side effects, and
dead flag elimination removed the flag computation and then the load
feeding it. The probes were gone: the stack pointer moved past the guard
page without a fault, and the first real store hit the uncommitted page
below it, an access violation on the lowest page of the stack instead of
STATUS_STACK_OVERFLOW. Both loads now count as having side effects, so
the pass keeps them.

